## 🛠️ OSS Stack & Deployment Blueprint

The production‑ready hybrid retrieval‑first & knowledge‑graph‑augmented generation stack is built around a minimal, opinionated set of open‑source components that together provide resilience, observability, and scalability while keeping operational overhead low.  The stack is intentionally lean: it relies on a single Java service that orchestrates retrieval from a Neo4j knowledge graph, calls an external LLM, and streams events via Kafka.  All cross‑cutting concerns are handled by Resilience4j, Axon, and Spring Kafka, while observability is achieved through OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Grafana, and Jaeger.  The deployment model is Kubernetes‑centric, with Helm charts for reproducible releases and ArgoCD for GitOps‑driven rollouts.

