@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/kg")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class KnowledgeGraphController {

    private final KnowledgeGraphService kgService;
    private final CircuitBreakerFactory circuitBreakerFactory;
    private final KafkaTemplate<String, KGEvent> kafkaTemplate;

    @PostMapping("/augment")
    public ResponseEntity<AugmentedResponse> augment(@RequestBody RetrievalPayload payload) {
        // 1️⃣ Guard downstream calls with Resilience4j circuit breaker
        Supplier<AugmentedResponse> supplier = CircuitBreaker
            .decorateSupplier(circuitBreakerFactory.create("kgService"), () -> enrich(payload));

        AugmentedResponse result = Try.ofSupplier(supplier)
            .recover(throwable -> fallback(payload))
            .get();

        // 2️⃣ Publish an event for replay / audit
        kafkaTemplate.send("kg-augmented", new KGEvent(payload.getQueryId(), result));

        return ResponseEntity.ok(result);
    }

    private AugmentedResponse enrich(RetrievalPayload payload) {
        // parse entities from LLM context, upsert them, then run a reasoning query
        List<String> entities = EntityExtractor.extract(payload.getContext());
        for (String e : entities) {
            kgService.upsertNode(new EntityNode(e));
        }
        List<RelationEdge> inferred = Reasoner.inferRelations(entities);
        inferred.forEach(kgService::upsertEdge);
        List<RelationEdge> subgraph = kgService.traverse(entities.get(0), 2);
        return new AugmentedResponse(payload.getQueryId(), subgraph);
    }

    private AugmentedResponse fallback(RetrievalPayload payload) {
        return new AugmentedResponse(payload.getQueryId(), Collections.emptyList());
    }
}
```

### 2. Architecture pattern – Resilience4j, Axon, Spring Kafka

The controller above demonstrates a classic **circuit‑breaker‑first** pattern: every call to `kgService` is wrapped by a Resilience4j `CircuitBreaker`. If the graph store becomes unavailable, the fallback returns an empty augmentation while the request still succeeds. Axon guarantees that every `NodeUpsertedEvent` and `EdgeUpsertedEvent` is persisted to an event store; Kafka mirrors those events to a topic (`kg-augmented`) enabling downstream analytics pipelines to replay the exact augmentation decisions.

